From: Karin-Laboratory contributors
Subject: [RFC PATCH] net: mediatek: quiesce FE recovery workers before cleanup
Upstream-base: torvalds/linux v6.18
Source-blob: e68997a29191b2a8ce0868873dcfe95c79e10e56

This is a source-only RFC for review. The current cleanup path frees
network devices before draining pending FE recovery work. Reorder the
existing synchronous cancellations ahead of the teardown calls.

This patch does NOT resolve the earlier mtk_remove() hardware-deinit
ordering, races with producers which can requeue the work, or possible
RTNL interactions. It is NOT validated by a kernel compile or runtime
testing. Do not use it as a standalone device fix.

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -4475,10 +4475,10 @@
 static int mtk_cleanup(struct mtk_eth *eth)
 {
+	cancel_work_sync(&eth->pending_work);
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&eth->reset.monitor_work);
 	mtk_sgmii_destroy(eth);
 	mtk_unreg_dev(eth);
 	mtk_free_dev(eth);
-	cancel_work_sync(&eth->pending_work);
-	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&eth->reset.monitor_work);
 
 	return 0;
 }
